      "statement": "All environment lookups funnel through the Environment utility in core/framework/common, backed by dotenv-java: if a .env file exists in the working directory it is loaded once and its values take precedence over system environment variables (missing values fall back to system env or null, and getEnvNonNull only logs an error), and the ArchUnit rule noGetEnv forbids every other class from calling System.getenv.",
